circular queue is the queue in which the last index of the the queue is logically connected to the first index of the queue 
circular queue is used to tackle the situation of false overflow which is despite being spaces in the queue it returns stack is full 
In circular queue if the rear exceeds the last index it again becomes the first index by the following code (rear+1)%max and similar with front
In circular queue the queue is full when the (rear+1)%max==front because there is already element there in a queue
in circular queue the queue is empty when the front ==-1 
